senses.gloss:
सम्-उच्चर, अस्, आ, अम्, going or coming forth
together; going upwards, ascending, flying upwards;
traversing.

समुत्क्लिश् सम्-उत्-क्लिश् (-उद्-क्˚), cl. 9. P.
-क्लिश्नाति, &c., to distress greatly, make very uneasy;
to suffer great uneasiness.

सम्-उत्पतन, अम्, n. the act of flying up toge-
ther, flying upwards, going upwards, ascending;
making effort, energy, exertion.

सम्-उद्धृत, अस्, आ, अम्, well raised or drawn
up or uplifted; picked up; completely drawn out or
extracted; lifted out, extricated; thrown up, vomited;
taken away, removed; taken out from (as a share),
deducted; set apart, divided; seized, possessed of;
ill-behaved.

सम्-उपागत, अस्, आ, अम्, gone near to, approached,
come together, assembled, met; come upon, incurred;
occurred, happening.

समुपवृंह् सम्-उप-वृंह्, Caus. -वृंहयति,
-यितुम्, to cause to increase, augment, strengthen;
to complete.

सम्-उब्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, confined, covered up;
injured; contracted, shrunk together, (Sāy. = सङ्-
कुचित.)

सम्-मुग्ध, अस्, आ, अम्, stupefied, astounded;
bewildered, fascinated; beautiful; (अम्), ind. in a
fascinating manner; furtively.
